      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T18:16:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving this out of init() has the same problem as the sandboxing, it allows vendor code to read environment variables without going through the APIs that let us add a dependency on them.",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca213faf_18fde288",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T00:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This breaks the intent of the sandbox.  As an init() function it is guaranteed to run before any init() functions in vendor plugins, as a function called from Main() it will be called much later and vendor plugins could access absolute paths.",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd351ac2_569b0928",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T07:32:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can\u0027t guarantee that this code runs after vendor plugin init functions this way, either, can you? My understanding is the only guarantee Golang gives is that if you import a package, its init() function is run before your init() function, which doesn\u0027t seem to be enough.\n\nIn that case, it would be better to set the cwd to \"/\" before running soong_build, wouldn\u0027t it? (it looks like it\u0027s easy to do, but the sandbox makes it non-trivial since it has its own ideas about what the cwd should be)",
      "parentUuid": "ca213faf_18fde288",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47578b82_aad05348",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T18:16:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you assume that vendor plugins have to interact with Soong and therefore must depend directly or transitively on the android package then the guarantee holds.  It is possible that vendors create a separate package with no dependencies and depend on both that package and the android package, in which case the ordering is not guaranteed at all by Go, but that is a relatively small hole that would take a very deliberate effort to bypass.\n\nChanging the directory before running soong_build is possible, but as you\u0027ve seen that gets tricky because Ninja is involved.  I think you could make that work though,  although it would still leave hiding environment variables as a problem that needs solving:\n- Set an environment variable in build/soong/ui/build/soong.go for the original build directory and the requested directory to cd to\n- Modify blueprint\u0027s rule to cd to that environment variable if it is set\n- Read the original build directory environment variable at the beginning of soong_build to save it, and clear it.  I think this still needs to happen in an init() function.",
      "parentUuid": "fd351ac2_569b0928",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e2a1e6e0_45b861be",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T18:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is exactly what https://android-review.googlesource.com/q/topic:soong-early-sandbox does, modulo the cleaning the environment variable part.\n\nI have to ask, though, do we need to sandbox partner plugins in this exact way? It looks like there is ample room to bypass the current setup, even accidentally (all it takes is a simple \"utility\" package)\n\nIOW, it looks odd that init() functions get so much scrutiny while the sandbox is leaky in all sorts of other ways. Or maybe I\u0027m overestimating its leakiness?",
      "parentUuid": "47578b82_aad05348",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6147e6a_78756aed",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T19:23:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An init() function in a utility package that does not import any Soong packages is the only leak I know of, and that seems pretty unlikely.  init() and global variable initializations are pretty common in Soong code to register module types and ninja variables, so making sure environment variables are properly hidden by then seems useful.\n\nStepping back a bit, what\u0027s your goal for refactoring this?  My suggestion in shared/debug.go to take the environment variable value as a parameter makes the refactoring unnecessary if all you want is to enable debugging soong_ui.\n\nAlso, unlike soong_build, soong_ui is not embedded in ninja.  You could implement delve support for soong_ui entirely within build/soong/soong_ui.bash, with no need to reexecute itself like soong_build does.",
      "parentUuid": "e2a1e6e0_45b861be",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98c12038_b3f6adb7",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-18T16:24:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TBH, my goal was just to make it possible to use Delve with soong_ui in a way that\u0027s mostly consistent with soong_build. Then I thought it makes sense to share the pertinent code, then init() skeleton fell out of the closet when I made soong_ui depend on the android package against which there were no guardrails. So I figured I could also fix that in one fell swoop.\n\nThe reason why I am suspicious about init() methods is my bad experiences with the corresponding concepts in Java (initializers of static class members) and C++ (static initialization order fiasco), then I looked at the semantics of init() and its semantics didn\u0027t convince me, either. But maybe I\u0027m just not familiar enough with Go idioms and that\u0027s how Gophers do it? (the Go style guide doesn\u0027t seem to say anything about the matter)\n\nI don\u0027t insist on this particular solution, but it looks like this and the soong-early-sandbox topic make life easier and remove a bit of magic, which is welcome *and* make the \"cd /\" sandbox more secure. \n\nWhat\u0027s the alternative?",
      "parentUuid": "d6147e6a_78756aed",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ddf1e8f_4c19fcee",
        "filename": "android/sandbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-18T22:02:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed on init() methods that do work generally being a bad idea, but we use them for plugin registraion, so they will be present.\n\nThe soong-early-sandbox topic is fine, but only solves half the problem, because you still have to do something about hiding environment variables before plugin init().  And if environment variables are hidden before init(), then ReexecWithDelveMaybe (and InitSandbox for that matter) can\u0027t read them directly, so you\u0027re back where you started.\n\nThe alternative is what I suggested in the comments in shared/debug.go.  With a few more details:\n* Leave android.ReexecWithDelveMaybe(), it\u0027s needed to get access to the sandbox environment variables.  Replace its implementation with a call to shared.ReexecWithDelveMaybe(soongDelveListen, soongDelvePath).\n* From soong_ui, call shared.ReexecWithDelveMaybe(os.Getenv(\"SOONG_UI_DELVE\"), os.Getenv(\"SOONG_DELVE_PATH\"))\n* In shared.ReexecWithDelveMaybe(), use the first argument for the listen address, and the second as the path to dlv, falling back to exec.LookPath(\"dlv\") if it is empty.",
      "parentUuid": "98c12038_b3f6adb7",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
