      "writtenOn": "2021-02-19T09:01:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, I went all the way and cleared the environment by calling \"env -i\" around soong_build in bootstrap.go (where I do \"cd /\" on the soong-early-sandbox topic)\n\nHowever, it turned out that that doesn\u0027t work because ctx.Config().Getenv() calls are all over the place in soong_build and that gets its data from config.env, which is a copy of originalEnv (see config.go:360)\n\nBut then what is the point of hiding the environment variables from partner plugins? It\u0027s that access to environment variables is tracked? That\u0027s useful, I guess, but that can still be used to do all sorts of shenanigans.",
      "parentUuid": "1ddf1e8f_4c19fcee",
      "revId": "4cb0220337bd98cd5b3cea8a8cf925e02971610e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
